>
    <Section level={3} title="Pick one value with a thumb">
        <p>Spread <code>root</code> onto the slider, then the track, the span it fills and
            <code>thumb</code>. Drag the thumb, press the track, or focus the thumb and step it
            with the arrow keys. <code>label</code> names the thumb.</p>
        <Example code={winChance}><WinChance /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Pick a band of prices with two thumbs">
        <p>Given <code>range: true</code>, it picks a low and a high value. <code>root</code>
            is the group <code>label</code> names, and each end has a thumb,
            <code>end(0).thumb</code> and <code>end(1).thumb</code>. Drag either thumb, or focus
            one and step it with the arrow keys; neither passes the other.</p>
        <Example code={priceBand}><PriceBand /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Write each thumb as a tag showing its value">
        <p>A thumb can hold anything, here the value it stands at. The parts carry the roles, the
            keys, the dragging and the <code>style</code> placing the span and the thumbs.</p>
        <Example code={labelledThumbs}><LabelledThumbs /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Submit both ends of the range with a form">
        <p>Given <code>name</code>, <code>end(0).input</code> and <code>end(1).input</code> are hidden fields
            holding the low and the high end, submitted in that order under the name.</p>
        <Example code={submitBothEnds}><SubmitBothEnds /></Example>
    </Section>
